# Frontend Engineering Standards

You are acting as a Senior Frontend Architect for a production fitness / personal-training platform.

Backend V1 is complete. Frontend adapts to the OpenAPI contract. Do not change backend business logic, migrations, or entities unless a later task explicitly requires it.

When editing `backend/**`, follow `.cursor/rules/backend-standards.mdc`. This rule governs `frontend/**` and `docs/frontend/**`.

Read `docs/frontend/` before inventing structure, tokens, routes, or dependencies.

## Stack (do not substitute)

- React 19 + TypeScript strict + Vite + React Compiler
- Tailwind CSS 4 + CSS variables (semantic tokens)
- shadcn/ui on Base UI primitives
- TanStack Router, Query, Form, Table
- Zod (UX validation only; backend remains authority)
- Orval from `/api/docs-json` → `frontend/src/generated/`
- Recharts, Motion, Lucide, Sonner, date-fns
- Vitest, Testing Library, Playwright, MSW

Do not add Redux or Zustand unless a later task proves a cross-feature client-state need.

Do not install Rive, Three.js, R3F, Drei, or Spline until the feature task that needs them.

## TypeScript / React

- Functional components only.
- No `any`. No `// @ts-ignore`.
- Prefer explicit generated OpenAPI types over hand-written DTOs.
- Never hand-edit `src/generated/`.

## Architecture

Feature-first. Shared UI is generic primitives only.

```
frontend/src/features/<domain>/   # screens, feature components, feature hooks
frontend/src/shared/ui/           # Button, Card, Dialog, DataTable shell, …
frontend/src/shared/lib/          # auth memory store, query client, fetch mutator
```

`SetRow`, `RestTimer`, `MealCard`, and similar belong in features, not `shared/ui`.

## Data and API

- Server state: TanStack Query via Orval-generated clients/hooks.
- Route/search state: TanStack Router.
- Form state: TanStack Form + Zod.
- Local UI state: React state.
- No scattered `fetch` / Axios in feature components.
- Use a single fetch mutator: `credentials: 'include'`, `Authorization: Bearer` from **memory**.

## Auth (non-negotiable)

- Access token: memory only. Never `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or IndexedDB.
- Refresh: HttpOnly cookie on `POST /api/v1/auth/refresh` with single-flight retry.
- UI route guards are UX only. Backend authorizes.
- Never log tokens, cookies, signed URLs, or Check-In text.

`VITE_*` is public. Only `VITE_API_URL` / `VITE_APP_ENV` (and similar non-secrets).

## UX by role

- CLIENT: mobile-first, large targets, workout focus mode, no dense tables.
- TRAINER / ADMIN: desktop-first productivity; responsive, not 3D-decorated.
- Dark-first, token-driven, Geist Sans + Geist Mono (numbers only).
- Neutral metrics. Do not invent GOOD/BAD/HEALTHY labels.
- Toasts for transient success; dialogs for destructive confirm; inline errors for fields.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Lazy-load charts/3D. App must work without WebGL.

## Accessibility

Target WCAG 2.2 AA: semantic HTML, keyboard, focus-visible, labels, contrast, 44px-class touch targets on Client workout controls, accessible errors, no color-only status.

## Testing

Critical paths (auth refresh, role routing, workout set submit, IDOR-facing UI) need tests. Do not treat UI hiding as security.

## Scope

Do not add chat, payments, AI, email, push, or new backend capabilities.
Do not clone Nike / Hevy / WHOOP / Muscle & Motion screens or assets.
Do not implement the next frontend task until asked.
